From db5ecd6b1947cd6026b1b89d725bd1986cc5f65f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:21:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] v31.3: bounded Apify wait + hard-killed re-entries count
 against the guard

- apify_service: call() waits at most actor_run_timeout + 90s (wait_duration);
  a run still READY/RUNNING afterwards is aborted and reported as a timeout.
  run_timeout only bounds a RUNNING Actor; a run parked in READY never
  reaches it and our worker blocked forever (runs 20260925T094032Z, ...065236947).
- run_manager: a worker that re-enters the adaptive step after a previous
  worker died inside it (stale-run resume, no graceful deadline hand-off)
  now counts as a continuation for MAX_ADAPTIVE_CONTINUATIONS_WITHOUT_PROGRESS.
- tests: test_v31_3_actor_wait_bound.py (4), HardKilledWorkerTest (1)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FM9VfoHhfyZmxPfBDYfQjP
